    "notes": "BRANCHLAB V0.2; safe fresh-process or Archil fresh-VM state handoff. No host crash or lost-AZ test. Local and Archil have different hardware. 'Fresh VM' reads do not measure a long-lived client's directory-cache TTL. A successful fsync + cross-VM read is not proof of catastrophic-host-failure durability. Each trial writes to unique isolated paths; independent writers never intentionally share files. No branches/checkpoints are created. Archil uses its default image; cleanup runs with a conditional mount via POST /api/exec; SQLite uses journal_mode=TRUNCATE (DELETE/WAL fail across execs, ARCHIL-FINDINGS.md #2). Archil commits a writing exec at exit, so a fresh-VM read after write-fsync cannot separate fsync durability from that exit commit."
